          %h2#statement_and_introduction Statement and introduction
          %p The Tychonoff theorem for locales states that a small product of compact locales is compact. Remarkably, and in stark contrast to the Tychonoff theorem for compact spaces, this result requires only constructive reasoning for its proof; in particular, the axiom of choice (or some other choice principle) is not needed.
          %p
            Our account of this result is adapted from
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#JV91"} Johnstone and Vickers
          %p
            The key result is the finitary case, that the product of
            %em two
            compact locales is compact, or equivalently that the coproduct of two compact frames is compact. For topological spaces the standard argument is well-known, and appears regularly in undergraduate courses, but crucially uses spatiality (existence of enough points) as a kind of “crutch”. The reader might like to try his or her own hand at proving this result for general locales where the crutch is no longer available, to appreciate that a somewhat different approach may be needed even for the finitary case.
          %h2#frames_and_the_category_of_suplattices Frames and the category of sup-lattices
          %p
            The category of locales is by definition opposite to the category of frames; following Joyal and Tierney, we consider frames as idempotent commutative monoids in the symmetric monoidal closed (smc) category
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_1.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sup
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sup
            consisting of sup-lattices.
          %p
            The category of frames is the full subcategory of the category of commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantales"} quantales
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_2.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Q
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Q, \cdot, 1)
            %em idempotent
            commutative quantales, meaning that
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_3.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \leq 1
            for all
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_4.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in Q
            (the quantale unit
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_5.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            is the top element
            = succeed ")," do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_6.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \top
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_7.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \cdot x = x
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_8.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in Q
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong (Joyal-Tierney)
              The coproduct of a collection of frames coincides with their coproduct in the category of commutative quantales.
          %p
            As commutative quantales are just commutative monoids in
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_9.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Sup
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Sup, \otimes)
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_10.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P, Q
            is given by the tensor product
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_11.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \otimes Q
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_12.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sup
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sup
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "/nlab/show/cocommutative+coalgebra#relation_to_cartesian_monoidal_categories"} here
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_13.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y
            is their sup-lattice tensor product
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_14.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \otimes Y
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_15.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sup
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sup
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Joyal-Tierney)
              The forgetful functor
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_16.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Frame
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sup
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Frame \to Sup
              preserves and reflects filtered colimits. Thus the coproduct of a family of frames
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_17.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{F_i\}_{i \in S}
              may be computed as
            .maruku-equation
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_18.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi colim
                      %mrow
                        %mi finite
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi F
                        %mo ⊆
                        %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi F
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{i \in S} F_i = colim_{finite\; F \subseteq S} \otimes_{i \in F} F_i
            %p where the colimit is over the filtered diagram of finite subsets and inclusions between them.
          %p Much of the proof of the Tychonoff theorem will be concentrated in explicit manipulations with sup-lattice tensor products; we turn to this next.
          %h2#symmetric_monoidal_closed_structure_for_suplattices Symmetric monoidal closed structure for sup-lattices
          %p
            The closed structure of
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_19.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sup
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sup
            has internal homs
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_20.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X, Y]
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_21.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_22.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ladj
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ladj(X, Y)
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_23.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a sup-lattice iff
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_24.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{op}
            is a sup-lattice), and it will be convenient also to consider
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_25.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Radj
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Radj(X, Y)
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_26.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
          %p
            We specially point out the sup-lattice
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_27.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2} = \{0 \leq 1\}
            (if we are generalizing from
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_28.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            to a topos, we use instead the subobject clasifier
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_29.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            which is an internal sup-lattice). This is the unit for the smc structure on
            = succeed ":" do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_30.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sup
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sup
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_31.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathbf{2}, X] \cong X
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_32.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}^{op}
            or
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_33.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{op}
            plays the role of dualizing object: homming into it, we calculate
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_34.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ladj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi Radj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi Ladj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi op
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ladj(X, \mathbf{2}^{op}) \cong Radj(\mathbf{2}^{op}, X)^{op} \cong Ladj(\mathbf{2}, X^{op}) \cong X^{op}.
          %p
            Here the first isomorphism takes a left adjoint
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_35.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: X \to \mathbf{2}^{op}
            to its right adjoint
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_36.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g: \mathbf{2}^{op} \to X
            in the opposite direction, and it also reverses 2-cells, i.e., takes an inequality
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_37.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi f
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \leq f'
            of left adjoints to a mated inequality
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_38.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g' \leq g
            of right adjoints. The second isomorphism is a case of taking a functor
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_39.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g: \mathbf{2}^{op} \to X
            to its opposite
            = succeed ";" do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_40.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mi op
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^{op}: \mathbf{2} \to X^{op}
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_41.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ladj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ladj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Ladj(Ladj(X, \mathbf{2}^{op}), \mathbf{2}^{op})
          %p is thus identified (up to canonical isomorphism) with
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_42.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi id
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi op
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi op
                  %mo =
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{id}{\to} X^{op\; op} = X
          %p
            making
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_43.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}^{op}
            a dualizing object: the smc category
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_44.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sup
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sup
            is a
            = succeed "-autonomous" do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_45.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_46.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Sup
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sup
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^\ast = (-)^{op}: Sup^{op} \to Sup
          %p
            Being a
            = succeed "-autonomous" do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_47.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_48.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ≅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi op
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \otimes Y \cong [X, Y^{op}]^{op}
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_49.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi Y
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi Ladj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi Ladj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Ladj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi Ladj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X \otimes Y)^{op} \cong Ladj(X \otimes Y, \mathbf{2}^{op}) \cong Ladj(X, Ladj(Y, \mathbf{2}^{op})) \cong Ladj(X, Y^{op}).
          %p
            This observation saves us from having to construct
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_50.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \otimes Y
            explicitly as a coequalizer of a free sup-lattice
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_51.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(X \times Y)
            (of
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_52.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}
            = succeed ")." do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_53.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times Y
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_54.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi Radj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \otimes Y \cong Radj(X^{op}, Y);
          %p
            this isomorphism takes
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_55.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \in X \otimes Y
            to the right adjoint
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_56.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi w
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_w: X^{op} \to Y
            defined by
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_57.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi w
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo :
                        %mi u
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi v
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi w
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_w(u) = \bigvee_{v: u \otimes v \leq w} v
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_58.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi Radj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \otimes Y \cong Radj(Y^{op}, X)
            taking
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_59.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \in X \otimes Y
            to a right adjoint
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_60.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi w
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi_w: Y^{op} \to X
            %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_61.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi w
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\phi_w, \psi_w)
            forms a contravariant Galois connection with
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_62.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi w
                      %mi op
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi_w^{op} \dashv \phi_w
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              Recall the classical proof that a product of two compact topological spaces
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_63.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y
              is compact. A standard lemma, sometimes called the
              = succeed "," do
                %em tube lemma
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_64.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              of
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_65.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times Y
              and any
              = succeed "," do
                %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_66.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_67.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              of
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_68.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              such that
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_69.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \times Y
              is finitely covered by
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_70.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math#mathml_8dc3bb6751048ae95b7ef38684e83fcda1a759e8_71.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \subseteq A
              covers
              = succeed ";" do
